  "behavior": [
    "Runtime.UpdateObservations owns callback preparation, cancellation, serialization, and publication. Runtime.ObservationInputs exposes immutable current and selected baseline snapshots without source reads or file writes.",
    "Empty and failed preparation preserve accepted state. Shutdown rejects a late callback result. Callbacks must not call another mutation on the same runtime.",
    "Unchanged projected provider fields require a permitted original provider, binding identity, and revision. Actual operator edits retain local field authority.",
    "The publication-order fixture now uses only its two reviewed definitions. Both store-entry deadlines and all original publication assertions remain unchanged."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "D24 reset scopes and CLI/HTTP runtime integration remain open. The existing CLI flag is --force; the Go option is sync.WithFresh. Its current pipeline still selects an empty baseline.",
    "Projected field checks do not prove account ownership or full selector identity. Scoped membership, field presence, reset masks, and full authority enforcement remain open.",
    "No request latency or allocation measurement, primary acceptance credit, branch push, native CI dispatch, GitHub merge, or release. Full repository verification and required pre-PR review remain open."
  ],
